WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.130
In Orbitals, check rows 26 and 27. Set the isovalue magnitude to 0.03 and the

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:14.000
grid to 128³, then generate both fields together.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:19.281
Saved surfaces lists one positive and one negative level for each orbital. Use

00:00:19.281 --> 00:00:23.750
the eye controls to show only one orbital at a time.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:30.350
This HOMO export uses levels of −0.03 and +0.03 per bohr to the three halves.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:34.750
Keep the same camera and image dimensions for the LUMO.

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:40.470
Select the LUMO and refresh the rendering key before the second PNG. The

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:45.310
four-row comparison CSV records both signed levels and the actual triangle

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:45.750
counts.
